      "content": "It's not advisable to pair high caffeine pre-workout supplements with a potential allergy. It might increase anxiety and discomfort, potentially worsening your symptoms. Try to remove the bar and take any necessary antiallergy medication prior to your workout. If you still want to have the pre-workout, technically, it's fair to drink a small amount of water or go for a short walk, but keeping an eye on your symptoms is key. Safety first—consider this as much as your exercise goals.",
