      "content": "It's positive that you're aware of your body, but even without a severe reaction, consuming a full dose of an energy supplement before a significant workout is not recommended. High doses of caffeine and pre-workouts can lead to increased heart rate, restlessness, and anxiety, potentially affecting performance rather than helping it. If you're feeling hesitant about the supplement due to a slight reaction, it's best to err on the side of caution. Use water as a placebo to help situate confidence in your workout. Skipping the pre-workout conservatively allows you to maintain intense focus without the risk of overstimulation. Listen to your body, and consider resting a day if your symptoms persist or worsen. Prioritize health and safety over a single intense lifting session.",
